+|BPR05|Payment documents/ledgers attached to the **October 28, 2001 Parkwood interview**, **EO14040-003828–003830**; original copies recorded in the case file's **1A section**|Interview acquired. Attachments not located/verified here; the next released page begins an unrelated telephone entry report. Obtain the attachment list, 1A inventory, receipt/custody records, originals/copies and check/deposit images. Test the $8 insurance/application-fee descriptions, $1,010 payment, and copying/re-stapling concern without presuming tampering.|
+|BPR06|Plaintiffs **Ex12A**, especially February 2–4 entries, and **Ex5 pp.197–198**; original Sprint/local-carrier returns, subscriber records and FBI TA import/analysis versions|FBI2005 table acquired; cited litigation table/expert pages and exact source cellular returns not acquired as identified records. Map each row's carrier, original timezone, units, direction and number-to-person attribution; test CBR/cell description and22/27 totals.|
+|BPR07|Original originating/receiving records for the Aulaqi-home call identified at **EO14040-002759**, plus averment §758 worksheet|Date remains April 19 in FBI report versus April 20 in pleading. Inspect native date/timezone fields, not an assumed conversion.|
+|BPR08|**July 18, 2007 EC EO14040-002797–002814** and its named **42-page frequency spreadsheet plus i2 charts**, original source returns/import logs|EC acquired; full named enclosure not separately identified/verified. Preserve the broader three-person/network scope and line-specific emphasis. Link chart edges back to carrier rows rather than treating them as additional independent evidence.|
+|BPR09|AT&T November 29, 2001 return and all pages for its **two accounts**, with redacted identifiers lawfully mapped; corresponding subpoena and December 27–28 data-loading artifacts, **EO14040-003831–003884** selected pages|Actual carrier pages and loading form acquired. Preserve the eight-rowJune23, 2000/42-billed-minute sample. Determine complete returned date windows/account linkage; do not generalize its18-month retention statement to other carriers or to later FBI custody.|
+|BPR10|Complete **August 4–6, 2003 Bayoumi FD-302**, transcribedAugust18, 2003, and exhibits identified in its FD-340 envelope; later plaintiffs **Ex91 declaration** and **Ex120 deposition** 440–447,737,452–454|Selected FD-302 pages acquired, including originalp.5. The released file jumps from cover to selected continuations; do not call it the full interview. Compare the $4,000–$8,000 recollection, return-to-office accounts and supplied cash against underlying records.|
+
+The existing S013 incomplete `02/2000` entry remains a separate target: original
+call record, EC working notes and source chronology. No day has been supplied by
+this tranche.
+
+## Retrieval coverage and gaps
+
+The preserved Motley Rice documents page links public briefs/averment, not the
+specific Ex550, KSAEx91 or Ex12A originals in the links inspected. Its evidence
+library snapshot exposes two document downloads (a hearing transcript and an
+opinion); neither is one of those exhibits. This is a finite page observation,
+not a claim that no further endpoint or public copy exists.
+
+Targeted indexed searches used the Bates/exhibit combinations `FBI8057`,
+`FBI2808`, `Ex12A`, Bank of America receipt/deposit-slip terms, and Bayoumi phone
+records. Those searches led to the FBI releases now acquired, but not to an
+independently acquired original of each named litigation exhibit. A direct
+CourtListener search returned403; a specific 2021 complaint PDF returned404.
+These access failures are not evidence of suppression, deletion or current docket
+sealing. Search snippets and a third-party mirror marked with protective-order
+language were not substituted for authenticated, cleared originals.
+
+The FBI's **redaction key** separately identifies privacy, judicial-authorization,
+law-enforcement and other restrictions. Blank/redacted identifiers cannot be
+filled by guessing. No private or sealed records were accessed, no payment was
+made and nobody was contacted. The original receipt and cellular-return acquisition
+task remains open; this publication records actual progress and the precise gaps.
